EF AI Workspace (#221): sidebar v5, owner-approved 2026-10-25 («موافق ابدأ التنفيذ»): «Customize» gathers every tool,
«More» is gone, and the phone drawer shows its sections on top. The owner's phone feedback: the bottom tab bar inside the
drawer went unnoticed and the floating «New chat» covered the history; the owner also wants a sidebar that takes future
sections without a redesign. Upstream has no customize page or sidebar configuration, so the page is EF's own and is
built from upstream's side-nav links: a section an upgrade adds appears there by itself.

- Rail (UnifiedSidebar/ExpandedPanel.tsx): «New chat», «Chats», a line, Projects and Documents, «Customize» (marked on
  its page, its tools' pages, the admins' marketplace, and while one of its panel tools holds the sidebar), the account.
  Skills and «More» (EfMoreMenu.tsx, deleted) move into «Customize».
- «Customize» (EfPages/EfCustomizePage.tsx, route /customize): a card per tool with one line on what it is for, the whole
  card its link. «For you»: ready commands, skills, memory, bookmarks, then any other section the deployment enables,
  marked «New» until described. «Admins only» (#189, #218): the marketplace with «New assistant» (a new chat with the
  builder open), the builder when the marketplace is off, the parameters, and the MCP servers named «Connectors». Panel
  tools open in the sidebar's panel through its hidden shortcut targets, as the keyboard shortcuts do, opening the
  sidebar or the phone drawer first. A tip on «/» and «$» in the message box.
- Tool pages (EfPages/EfSectionPage.tsx; skills, ready commands, memory, bookmarks): a breadcrumb back to «Customize»
  above the title, a back button on phones.
- Phone drawer (UnifiedSidebar/EfChatsPanel.tsx): «Baseer» and the X, the search, three tiles (Projects, Documents,
  Customize), «Chats» with the sort and filter menu, the chips and the history, and «New chat» docked at the bottom
  beside the account (keeping upstream's test id, which focus falls back to). No tab bar, no floating button.
- Sections (UnifiedSidebar/efSidebar.ts): EF_PAGES.customize, EF_CUSTOMIZE_FIRST, efCustomizeLinks (was efMoreLinks),
  efCustomizeIsCurrent; «mcp-builder» reads «Connectors».
- Strings (en/translation.json; ar.json): «Customize», its hint, headings, tip and descriptions, «New», «New assistant»,
  «Connectors», «Back to {{0}}», «Breadcrumb»; «More» removed.
- Tests: ExpandedPanel.spec (rail order and «Customize» marking), EfCustomizePage.spec (employee and admin cards, a new
  section, panel tools, «New assistant»), EfSectionPage.spec (the way back).

